29:44.020 --> 29:46.520
and look at the final composite shift

29:46.520 --> 29:47.120
they produce.

29:47.120 --> 29:47.600
SGD. Okay.

29:48.020 --> 29:49.240
SGD. By comparing the direction

29:49.240 --> 29:51.000
of the composite H-step shift

29:51.000 --> 29:52.220
against the direction

29:52.220 --> 29:54.540
of the true instantaneous global gradient

29:54.540 --> 29:55.660
at the reference point,

29:55.800 --> 29:57.720
you can mathematically measure

29:57.720 --> 29:59.080
the angular divergence.

29:59.580 --> 30:00.720
SGD. Ah, I see.

30:01.160 --> 30:02.440
So if the composite vector

30:02.440 --> 30:04.400
