30:19.620 --> 30:21.020
SGD. It provides real observability.

30:21.580 --> 30:22.160
But you know,

30:22.220 --> 30:23.380
it leads to a much more difficult

30:23.380 --> 30:25.340
structural question regarding trust.

30:25.420 --> 30:26.020
SGD. Oh, absolutely.

30:26.580 --> 30:27.080
SGD. Like,

30:27.420 --> 30:28.280
if the architecture

30:28.280 --> 30:30.180
is this inherently fragile,

30:30.820 --> 30:32.700
if it requires tagged summaries

30:32.700 --> 30:33.920
to prevent rooting graphs

30:33.920 --> 30:35.160
from double counting vectors,

30:35.740 --> 30:36.920
and if it requires

30:36.920 --> 30:38.340
asynchronous null logic

30:38.340 --> 30:39.200
to handle latency,

30:39.880 --> 30:41.460
and if it is mathematically

30:41.460 --> 30:42.460
guaranteed to drift

30:42.460 --> 30:43.680
under heterogeneity,

30:44.220 --> 30:45.620
how can the end user

30:45.620 --> 30:46.520
ever actually trust

30:46.520 --> 30:47.700
the final model artifact

30:47.700 --> 30:48.200
they're given?

30:48.540 --> 30:48.560
SGD. Right.

30:49.320 --> 30:50.520
And this is where Flyxion

30:50.520 --> 30:51.580
introduces the concept

30:51.580 --> 30:52.980
of the commit certificate.

30:53.840 --> 30:55.400
It's essentially a final,

30:55.720 --> 30:56.460
formal proof

30:56.460 --> 30:57.460
of the model's construction.

30:58.300 --> 30:59.340
SGD. The commit certificate.

30:59.540 --> 30:59.780
Mm-hmm.

30:59.780 --> 31:01.020
SGD. It's envisioned

31:01.020 --> 31:03.300
