tensors, directed

37:32.360 --> 37:33.340
acyclic graphs,

37:33.800 --> 37:34.920
and the mathematics

37:34.920 --> 37:35.760
of objective

37:35.760 --> 37:36.680
inconsistency.

37:36.680 --> 37:37.280
A lot of heavy

37:37.280 --> 37:37.640
math.

37:38.060 --> 37:39.000
But the core

37:39.000 --> 37:39.700
finding here,

37:40.180 --> 37:40.820
that systems

37:40.820 --> 37:41.720
permanently drift

37:41.720 --> 37:42.400
toward biased

37:42.400 --> 37:43.080
outcomes when

37:43.080 --> 37:43.720
local nodes

37:43.720 --> 37:44.700
operate independently

37:44.700 --> 37:45.460
for too long

37:45.460 --> 37:46.740
on local data,

37:47.280 --> 37:48.520
that is not just

37:48.520 --> 37:49.100
a property of

37:49.100 --> 37:49.840
silicon and code.

37:50.000 --> 37:50.320
No.

37:50.960 --> 37:51.720
What does this

37:51.720 --> 37:52.600
mathematical law

37:52.600 --> 37:53.280
mean for

37:53.280 --> 37:54.620
decentralized human

37:54.620 --> 37:55.220
organizations?

37:56.080 --> 37:57.300
We exist in an

37:57.300 --> 37:58.140
era of remote

37:58.140 --> 37:59.200
work, globally

37:59.200 --> 38:00.040
distributed teams,

38:00.220 --> 38:01.080
and decentralized

38:01.080 --> 38:01.680
autonomous

38:01.680 --> 38:02.360
organizations.

38:02.360 --> 38:03.940
If a human

38:03.940 --> 38:04.740
team goes too

38:04.740 --> 38:05.440
long without a

38:05.440 --> 38:06.580
true, synchronous

38:06.580 --> 38:07.800
alignment, if we

38:07.800 --> 38:08.820
just sit in our

38:08.820 --> 38:09.940
isolated silos,

38:10.520 --> 38:11.320
optimizing solely

38:11.320 --> 38:12.260
for our local

38:12.260 --> 38:13.240
KPIs and our

38:13.240 --> 38:14.280
local perspectives,

38:14.680 --> 38:15.960
do we suffer from

38:15.960 --> 38:16.640
the exact same

38:16.640 --> 38:17.500
mathematical drift?

38:17.960 --> 38:18.700
We probably do.

38:19.460 --> 38:20.100
Do our human

38:20.100 --> 38:20.820
teams fundamentally

38:20.820 --> 38:21.640
lose the shared

38:21.640 --> 38:22.100
objective?

38:22.500 --> 38:23.380
Not because any

38:23.380 --> 38:24.420
individual is acting

38:24.420 --> 38:25.800
maliciously, and

38:25.800 --> 38:26.460
not because our

38:26.460 --> 38:27.280
communication tools

38:27.280 --> 38:28.620
are broken, but

38:28.620 --> 38:29.360
simply because the

38:29.360 --> 38:30.300
geometry of our

38:30.300 --> 38:31.500
isolated, independent

38:31.500 --> 38:33.360
horizons inevitably

38:33.360 --> 38:34.220
warps the

38:34.220 --> 38:34.900
collective goal.

38:35.800 --> 38:36.440
If you are

38:36.440 --> 38:37.360
building a skyscraper

38:37.360 --> 38:38.500
with teams scattered

38:38.500 --> 38:40.000
across the globe, and

38:40.000 --> 38:40.700
you only sync up

38:40.700 --> 38:42.000
once a month, it

38:42.000 --> 38:42.820
isn't the blueprints

38:42.820 --> 38:43.460
you need to worry

38:43.460 --> 38:43.720
about.

38:44.080 --> 38:44.520
It is the

38:44.520 --> 38:45.400
mathematical certainty

38:45.400 --> 38:46.320
that, without

38:46.320 --> 38:47.600
continuous global

38:47.600 --> 38:49.160
synchronization, you

38:49.160 --> 38:49.960
are guaranteed to

38:49.960 --> 38:50.640
build a lopsided

38:50.640 --> 38:50.940
tower.

